FIRST PROJECT
To start with, I figured I would login to Kali with my fancy new AD credentials (username@DOMAIN.EXAMPLE in the username field) and try to get a network map with Zenmap. I used the default nmap -A -T4 scan, with the network info added in to the end of the command. I won't show the image here, but I will say it successfully found the other hosts (the server and the Windows 10 machine (this is before I realized I needed Ubuntu for Wazuh, so it wasn't on the network yet)), identified open ports, and identified the OS (within reasonable margin of error). It gives a nice rundown of everything it finds under Host Details of each host (which can be found on the left pane). Overall, very neat way to map my own network and see what it's got going on. It will likely be a big help in future projects to be able to refer back to this topology.
